Heap sort builds a max-heap and moves the maximum to the end; a min-heap yields
descending order
ts-heap-sort   lens: ordering   level: L3   family: ts-heap-patterns
Prerequisites: ts-heap-invariant. Follow-up: ts-heap-median. Complexity: O(n log n).
 Common misconception. Using a min-heap and swapping the root to the end sorts ascending.
Each extraction moves the root to the end of the array. If the root is the smallest value the array ends up in
descending order. Heap sort in place needs a max-heap: build it, then repeatedly swap the root with the last unsorted
slot and sift down over the shrunken range. It runs in O(n log n) with O(1) extra space.
